Z||000005||Master_Sushi||11-05-2001||06:19 PM||||Fieros never do donuts "that" well. Mid engine dosent help, you get allot of traction because of this. The stock powerplants arn't exactly torque monsters either.<P>To do anything close to those videos, I'll have to wait tell this winter after it snows. Nothing more fun then a small RWD car in a big empty parking lot!<P>For great tire roasting fun you need a front engine and a big V8. Thats why Mustangs and F-Bodys are ultimate dunut,tire smoking, burnout cars!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> I'm sure everybody knew this allready though.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Master_Sushi (edited 11-05-2001).]||||reg||10
